## 6. Module specifications

### 6.1 Resume & Skill-Gap Analyzer
- Parse PDF/DOCX → clean text → section detection (education, experience, projects, skills, certifications).
- Skill extraction: curated skills taxonomy + spaCy matcher + embedding fallback for near-matches.
- **Semantic match**: sentence-transformer embeddings of resume sections vs job description; cosine similarity per section and overall.
- **Skill gap** = JD required skills not covered (exact or semantic), ranked by importance weight.
- **ATS checks** (rule-based, explainable): standard section headings, parseable text, contact info present, length, bullet and metric usage, keyword coverage. Output 0-100 plus a fix-it list with reasons.
- Output must explain *why* each score moved. No black-box single number.
- Evaluation: build a small labeled set (manually annotated resume-JD pairs) and report precision/recall of skill-gap detection and rank correlation with human judgment.

### 6.2 Placement Readiness Predictor
- Features: CGPA, backlogs, 10th/12th %, internships, project count/complexity, certifications, coding stats, quiz scores, resume score, mock-interview averages, target company type.
- Models: Logistic Regression (baseline), Random Forest, XGBoost/LightGBM; pick by cross-validated results, then **calibrate probabilities**.
- Stratified k-fold CV; hold-out test set; guard against leakage (no features that are consequences of placement).
- Report accuracy, F1, ROC-AUC, calibration curve. Include an **ablation: academics-only vs full feature set** (literature suggests academic-only is much weaker; verify on our data).
- Explainability: SHAP per prediction, show top positive/negative drivers in the UI.
- Fairness check across department and gender where data allows; document in `docs/EVALUATION.md`.
- Serve via `registry.py` with versioned artifacts; retrain script; every score stores `model_version`.

### 6.3 AI Mock Interview Engine
- Question bank by role, company type, difficulty (HR, behavioral, technical-conceptual, DSA verbal explanation).
- Session flow: pick role → ask question → capture answer (text or audio) → score → feedback → next.
- STT with faster-whisper. Speech features with librosa: speaking rate (WPM), pause ratio, filler-word rate, pitch variability.
- **Content score**: embedding similarity to rubric/reference key points plus keyword/concept coverage; optional LLM-as-judge behind a feature flag (document cost and determinism limits).
- Output sub-scores: **confidence/delivery**, **communication**, **content correctness**, with specific, actionable feedback.
- Facial analysis (MediaPipe/FER, in-browser or server) is **stretch**, off by default, consent-gated, and must be labeled as indicative only.
- Evaluation: compare automated scores with human-rated samples (target correlation reported honestly, e.g. Pearson r).

### 6.4 Personalized Recommendation Engine
- Skill graph with prerequisites and per-company skill weights (product-based: DSA, system design, projects; service-based: aptitude, communication, fundamentals).
- Mastery tracking per skill: MVP **Bayesian Knowledge Tracing** updated from quiz/coding/interview events; stretch **DKT (LSTM)** trained and validated on ASSISTments, then adapted.
- Recommendation = rank of `gap_size × skill_weight × prerequisite_readiness`, with diversity and a "why this" reason string; resources from `learning_resources`.
- Closed loop: accepting/ignoring/completing a recommendation is logged and feeds back into mastery and ranking.

### 6.5 Readiness Score Aggregator
- Composite 0-100: weighted blend of predictor probability, resume score, skill mastery, interview score, consistency (activity). Weights configurable per company type and stored with each score for auditability.
- Score history, trend, and "what changed since last time" diff.

## 7. Product surfaces

**Student app:** onboarding + consent, profile builder, resume upload and report, target company/role selector, assessments and coding log, mock interview room, readiness dashboard (score, trend, skill radar, top gaps, SHAP drivers), personalized plan with weekly tasks, data export/delete page.

**Coordinator app:** cohort overview (score distribution, department heatmap), at-risk list (consented only), skill-gap aggregates, drive-readiness filters per company, CSV export, announcement/notifications.

**Admin:** job description library, question bank, skills taxonomy, learning resources, model versions, audit log.

Accessibility and UX: responsive, keyboard accessible, clear loading/error states, no dark patterns around consent.

## 8. Phased delivery (stop after each phase)

**Phase 0: Foundations.** Repo scaffold, Docker Compose, CI (lint, types, tests), `CLAUDE.md`, `.env.example`, health endpoint, frontend shell.
*Done when:* `docker compose up` runs api/web/db/redis; CI green.

**Phase 1: Auth, data model, consent.** Migrations, JWT auth with roles, profile CRUD, consent management, data export/delete, audit log.
*Done when:* role-based access tests pass; consent revoke removes dependent data access.

**Phase 2: Resume pipeline.** Upload, parsing, skill extraction, ATS rules, JD library, semantic match, gap report UI.
*Done when:* sample resumes produce stable, explainable reports; evaluation script reports metrics on the labeled set.

**Phase 3: Assessments and activity.** Quiz engine, coding log (manual/CSV), project/certification entry, event logging.
*Done when:* attempts persist and emit `events` used downstream.

**Phase 4: Readiness predictor.** Dataset prep, training pipeline, CV + ablation, calibration, SHAP, model registry, inference API, UI card.
*Done when:* `docs/EVALUATION.md` has real measured metrics and the ablation; predictions carry `model_version`.

**Phase 5: Mock interview.** Question bank, session flow, STT, speech features, content scoring, feedback UI. Facial analysis only if time permits.
*Done when:* an end-to-end session yields sub-scores and feedback; human-rating comparison script exists.

**Phase 6: Recommendation engine.** Skill graph, BKT mastery, ranking, reasons, feedback loop; DKT experiment as stretch.
*Done when:* recommendations change measurably after new attempts; offline replay test passes.

**Phase 7: Aggregator and dashboards.** Composite score, history, student dashboard, coordinator dashboard with consent-aware views.
*Done when:* new data triggers rescoring via worker and the UI reflects it.

**Phase 8: Evaluation and pilot harness.** Metrics suite, synthetic cohort generator (labeled synthetic), pilot onboarding flow, reporting notebook.
*Done when:* one command regenerates all evaluation tables/figures into `docs/EVALUATION.md`.

**Phase 9: Hardening and release.** Rate limiting, input validation, file-type/size limits and malware-safe handling, backups, load smoke test, security review checklist, deployment docs, demo seed data.
*Done when:* CI green, threat-model checklist complete, one-command demo works.

## 9. Targets (benchmarks from the literature, not guarantees)

Use as reference lines in `EVALUATION.md`; report whatever our data actually achieves:
- Readiness prediction accuracy in the high-70s to mid-80s % range on comparable data.
- Resume-to-role match accuracy near 79% in the cited transformer work.
- Mock-interview automated vs human rating correlation r ≥ 0.75 in cited work.
- Knowledge-tracing AUC around 0.86 on ASSISTments in the original DKT paper.

If our results fall short, say so, and document why (data size, label noise, features).

## 10. Non-functional requirements

- p95 API latency under 500 ms for non-ML endpoints; ML jobs async with status polling.
- Reproducible training: fixed seeds, pinned dependencies, data version hashes.
- Observability: structured logs, request IDs, basic metrics endpoint.
- Test coverage target: 80% backend services, key flows covered by e2e.
- Security: OWASP basics, password hashing (argon2/bcrypt), CORS allowlist, secrets via env, upload scanning/limits, PII never logged.

